  "summary": "Ganjifa, Ganjapa or Gânjaphâ, is a card game and type of playing cards that are most associated with Persia and India.",
  "description": "Ganjifa, Ganjapa or Gânjaphâ, is a card game and type of playing cards that are most associated with Persia and India. After Ganjifa cards fell out of use in Iran before the twentieth century, India became the last country to produce them. The form prevalent in Odisha is Ganjapa.",
  "culturalContext": "Registered as a Geographical Indication of India (handicraft, Karnataka; registration 2007–08), which protects the name for products made in its place of origin by traditional methods.",
